 @MLWJ1993  They did have that problem. Just because the frame time spikes weren't exactly the same doesn't mean they don't exist. It's a flawed test. The most likely reason it wasn't as bad is because Nvidia's APIs have more CPU overhead, slightly alleviating this problem that affects stronger CPUs more.

Check out the Gamers Nexus piece titled: GTA V Stuttering Mystery.

Then you can stop being such an Nvidia fanboy turd.

