Your assumption everyone favours a certain company because a result was more favourable to that company is absurd though.

 @Hehehe-hf7rq  I mean, most monitor/tvs being sold are 4k. I haven't seen people but as much 2k.  Bang for buck would be the 3070. Gets you 4k solid and it's powerful enough to test RTX. 
I only see that if you are still with a 1080 monitor AMD makes sense. 
You do get better performance with AMD on 1080. But...is 1080 the future? I don't think so.

 @vherostar  
Total nonsense. Nvidia introduced ray tracing 2 years ago and in that time only a handful of games support it. We're talking literally 6 or so games total that support both RT and dlss (and dlss is basically required to make RT playable). At the current rate there will be maybe 5-7 more games in another 2 years.

Lets be honest, RT is a bit of a joke right now. It's a matter of slightly better shadows and reflections for half or less the performance. The hardware simply isn't powerful enough for real meaningful RT implementation, maybe in another couple generations.

@JeremyCuddles TL:DR - AMD drivers are NOT bugged for 5000 series. 6000 series appears similar. Until I can get my hands on one here's my 5600xt experience for anyone considering a ~2060 level upgrade:

 @yanndsal  I bought a 5600 xt a month ago as a xmas gift. I stress tested it for 3 days: zero stability issues, zero driver issues. The SW is so nice IMO, and despite the reputation AMD earned in the past for 'bunches of driver issues', everything was just perfect. I gamed for three days on it: death stranding, apex, csgo, alyx, boneworks, trover, you get the idea. I played everything. Only one crash occurred, and it was a soft crash to desktop. I was overclocking and undervolting aggressively, crash ignored. Anyhow all of this is to say: I've been building PC's since the 90's and this was for sure the single best, most error-free GPU swap in my entire life. Don't let the idea of driver issues push you away from the 5000 & 6000 series AMD parts
(Swapped from a GTX 1060 6GB btw, & the 5600xt easily doubled my framerate and more, and @ higher settings. 5600xt is the real price/perf. king right now. Was $250 after rebate)
